data.content:
In .NET 10 (EF Core 10), the Cosmos DB provider already defaulted to async-only, but you could opt back in to sync-over-async behavior. **In .NET 11 (EF Core 11), that opt-in is removed entirely.** All synchronous LINQ operators — `ToList()`, `First()`, `Count()` — and `SaveChanges()` will throw `InvalidOperationException` against the Cosmos provider.

**Every method in your repository breaks.** The fix is to go fully async:

```csharp
public class ProductRepository
{
    private readonly CosmosDbContext _context;

    public async Task<List<Product>> GetAllAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.ToListAsync();
    }

    public async Task<Product> GetByIdAsync(int id)
    {
        return await _context.Products.FirstAsync(p => p.Id == id);
    }

    public async Task<int> GetCountAsync()
    {
        return await _context.Products.CountAsync();
    }

    public async Task SaveAsync(Product product)
    {
        _context.Products.Add(product);
        await _context.SaveChangesAsync();
    }
}
```

**Key changes:**
- Return `Task<T>` / `Task`, mark methods `async`
- `ToList()` → `ToListAsync()`, `First()` → `FirstAsync()`, `Count()` → `CountAsync()`, `SaveChanges()` → `SaveChangesAsync()`
- Rename methods with `Async` suffix by convention
- All callers up the chain must also be updated to `await` these methods

The async LINQ methods are in `Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore` (via `EntityFrameworkQueryableExtensions`), so no new package is needed.
